Stand-alone build guide for the developer agent. Read fully. Follow strictly.

19 November 2026

Table of Contents
PART 0 — HOW TO USE THIS DOCUMENT
0.1 Purpose
This document is the single source of truth for building the Sahatna prototype: a male reproductive-health companion for the UAE. It covers what to build, how to build it, how data is stored, how every backend stage works, how the user is guided, and how each failure is handled so that no flow breaks the chain.

0.2 Rules for the developer agent
Build exactly what is written. Where this document says “VERIFY”, check the linked official page and record the result in docs/verification-log.md. Do not guess.
Every stage of every flow has a defined failure state and a user message (Part 12). A stage may never end in a crash, a blank screen or a silent stop.
Work in the phase order of Part 15. Do not start a later phase until the acceptance criteria of the earlier one pass.
Where the product specification (the earlier Sahatna specification) provides content, use it as-is: the 26-question questionnaire in 5 blocks with “Prefer not to say”, the 74-day plan templates, and the clinician-approved urgent-care text. This document defines structure, not clinical content. Never invent clinical content.
Plain language in every user-facing text. Calm, hopeful tone for anything about pain, worry or abnormal results.
0.3 The four design rules (fixed, not negotiable)
#
Rule
What it means in the build
R1
We do not provide an exact sperm count to users.
Results are bands only: Low / Typical / Unclear for concentration and for motility. No number such as “42 million/mL” is ever shown for a home video. A number is shown only when it is copied from the user’s own laboratory report, labelled “from your lab report”.
R2
No single fertility score.
The only summary is the 3-colour bar (Green / Yellow / Red) with the reason. It shows urgency and next step. It is not a fertility percentage.
R3
The app is a pre-screen, not a laboratory replacement.
Every result screen says so in one plain sentence. Critical results route directly to a diagnostic centre.
R4
We never claim or promise 100% accuracy.
Our goal is the best accuracy we can reach. We publish measured performance after validation. Until validated, results carry the label “Prototype pre-screen”. The word “accurate” is never used without a measured, dated figure.
