PART 3 — ACCOUNTS, SIGN-IN AND CONSENT
3.1 Account design
The user chooses language, then gets a random username (for example “BlueFalcon-4821”) generated by the server. No real name is requested anywhere.
Sign-in uses Entra External ID with OIDC authorization-code flow and PKCE through the system browser. Recovery uses email or phone, optional, set by the user in Settings. If the user sets none, the app warns clearly: “If you lose this phone and have no recovery method, we cannot restore your account.”
The app never stores passwords. Tokens are stored in Keychain (iOS) or Keystore (Android) via expo-secure-store or react-native-keychain.
The server maps (issuer, subject) to an internal random UserId. All queries use UserId from the validated token, never from the client.
3.2 Consent centre (F3)
