PART 4 — DATA MODEL AND STORAGE
4.1 Principles
SQL is the source of truth for structured records. No spreadsheet is ever a data store.
Every health fact carries source (user, report, device, semen_pipeline, clinician), status (confirmed, unconfirmed, unknown, outdated), observed_at_utc, local_date, time_zone, unit.
Missing is NULL, never zero. Unknown, estimated and missing are different states.
Nothing is overwritten. A new answer, report or run creates a new record. History is kept.
Every table row has user_id and the API filters by it. Row-Level Security in SQL is added as defence in depth, not as the only control.
