4.4 The “vault” in simple words
The vault is the combination of the report-originals, report-json containers and the report_values / report_summaries tables. A user’s vault holds: the uploaded file, the full extraction JSON, the confirmed summary, and an index by test and date. The agent reads only from confirmed summary data through a fixed tool (Section 7.3).

PART 5 — REPORT VAULT: UPLOAD, PRIVACY, SUMMARY, STORAGE, RETRIEVAL
5.1 What the user sees (guide, in order)
Screen “Add a report”. Plain text: “Add your lab results so the assistant can use real values. You decide what to show.”
Privacy note (always shown before upload): “Your report may show your name, date of birth, ID or phone number. You do not need to share these. Before you upload, you can fold the top of the paper, cover that part with your hand or a paper, or crop it in the app. You can also upload the full report if you prefer. We store a private copy only if you agree.”
Choice: Take a photo / Choose a file (PDF, JPG, PNG) / Crop first. A crop tool lets the user black out the personal area. The app records privacy_mode as folded or full (user’s choice, for transparency only).
Upload progress with the states of Section 5.3.
Check screen (mandatory): the original image on one side, extracted rows on the other. Every row shows: test name, value, unit, reference range, flag, and confidence. The user taps “Matches” or edits the value. A field with low confidence is highlighted yellow. The user must confirm before saving.
Save: “Nothing becomes part of your health record until you confirm it.”
Done screen: summary card (date of report, lab name if visible, key values) and a button “Ask about this report”.
5.2 Pipeline (backend)
Client -> POST /v1/reports (metadata, consent check, quota)
      -> upload stream to quarantine blob
Worker 1: file validation (type by signature, size, page count, password check)
Worker 2: malware scan (use Microsoft Defender for Storage if available in region, else ClamAV container; VERIFY)
Worker 3: personal-data masking step (optional, see 5.4)
Worker 4: OCR/layout: Azure AI Document Intelligence (prebuilt-layout/read)
Worker 5: structuring: rule-based parser first; LLM structuring second (de-identified text only)
Worker 6: auto-checks: units, ranges, arithmetic (total = concentration x volume), date sanity
Worker 7: write report_values (unconfirmed) + extraction.json to vault
Client check screen -> user confirms -> PATCH /v1/reports/{id}/confirm
Worker 8: build summary.json + plain-text summary from CONFIRMED values only
Worker 9: write observations; index for agent retrieval

5.3 State machine
Created -> Receiving -> Quarantined -> Scanning -> Extracting -> NeedsUserReview -> Confirmed -> Summarised
                         |              |              |
                         +-> Rejected   +-> Rejected    +-> ExtractionFailed -> ManualEntry (user types values) -> NeedsUserReview

State
User message
Receiving
“Your report is uploading securely.”
Scanning
“We are checking the file.”
Extracting
“We are reading your report. You can leave this screen.”
NeedsUserReview
“Please check each value against your report.”
