Rules:

plain_text_summary is generated from the values by a template. An LLM may reword it, but a validator then checks that every number and date in the reworded text exists in values. If not, the template text is used.
Reference ranges are stored as written by the lab. We do not replace them with our own.
Unknown fields stay null.
The summary is versioned. If the user later corrects a value, a new summary version is written and the old one kept.
5.6 Retrieval by the agent
The agent has one tool, get_report_summary(doc_id | type, date_range), that:

Checks the reports_ai consent on the server.
Returns only confirmed_by_user = true values.
Returns value, unit, date, flag, reference range, source report id.
Never returns names, IDs or the original file.
The agent must cite the report date in each answer: “In your report from 3 October 2026, concentration was 14.2 million/mL (lab reference 16 or more).”

5.7 Conflict handling
If a report value conflicts with a questionnaire answer or an earlier report, both stay visible with dates, and the app asks “Which is current?”. It never overwrites silently.

PART 6 — HOME SEMEN PRE-SCREEN (CORE FEATURE F8)
6.1 What it is, and what it is not
It is a guided pre-screen. The user records short videos of a semen sample in a fixed-depth chamber under magnification. The system returns two bands (concentration and motility), each Low / Typical / Unclear, a 3-colour next-step bar, and a route to a lab when needed.

It is not a laboratory replacement (R3), it gives no exact count (R1), no fertility score (R2), and no accuracy promise (R4). Morphology (sperm shape) and DNA damage are not read from the video. If the user has a lab report with those values, the vault shows them as “from your lab report”.

