6.8 Models and algorithms
Detection. Preferred: a lightweight detector (YOLOX-s or RT-DETR, both Apache-2.0) fine-tuned on the VISEM-Tracking dataset (CC BY 4.0; 20 patients, 400x phase-contrast videos, annotated boxes and tracks; VERIFY the licence at https://datasets.simula.no/visem-tracking/) and then on our own pilot videos from clip-on and microscope setups. Do not use Ultralytics YOLO in a distributed product unless the commercial licence is bought (AGPL-3.0). Export to ONNX. Run with ONNX Runtime on CPU first.

Classical fallback (must exist; keeps the chain working before any custom model is trained). Background subtraction and difference of Gaussians to find small bright or dark blobs of expected size (using µm/pixel when known), Kalman filter and Hungarian assignment for tracks. This fallback is also used when the detector’s confidence on the clip is low. It is less accurate and the result is labelled accordingly in the audit record.

Tracking. ByteTrack or OC-SORT (MIT). Keep tracks of at least 1 second (30 frames).

Motility measures. Per track: VCL, VSL, VAP, straightness STR = VSL/VAP. Default classes (configurable, clinical advisor to confirm; VERIFY against WHO manual and CASA conventions): progressive if VAP at or above 25 µm/s and STR at or above 0.8; non-progressive if moving but not progressive; immotile if VAP under 5 µm/s. If calibration is missing, only “moving versus not moving” is used.

Concentration estimate (internal only). For each usable field: mean number of detected heads per frame divided by (field area x chamber depth), averaged across fields. The internal record keeps the estimate and a confidence interval from the spread across fields. These numbers are never sent to the user’s app (R1).

Banding rule (internal). Reference lower limits (WHO 6th edition, 2021): concentration 16 million/mL; total motility 42%; progressive motility 30%. VERIFY at https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240030787.

Concentration: Low if the upper end of the confidence interval is below 16. Typical if the lower end is at or above 16. Otherwise Unclear.
Motility: Low if the upper end of the interval for progressive motility is below 30%. Typical if the lower end is at or above 30%. Otherwise Unclear.
If fewer than 200 cells were assessed in total (WHO precision rule of thumb) the interval is wider, so more results fall in Unclear. This is intended: Unclear is a valid, safe answer.
Room temperature widens the motility interval by a configured amount.
If a model’s calibration error exceeds the validated limit, or the input is outside the training conditions (out-of-distribution check), the band is Unclear.
Models are versioned. semen_runs.model_version and pipeline_version are saved with every run. A model can be disabled with a feature flag, and the system falls back to Unclear without a code release.

Numeric leakage test (mandatory). An automated test inspects every API response and every client log for numeric concentration, percent motility or velocity values from the pipeline. If found, the build fails (R1).

