6.12 Validation programme (to switch from Prototype to Validated mode)
Required before the word “validated” appears anywhere:

Protocol approved by the ethics route a UAE clinic partner requires (DoH Abu Dhabi: https://www.doh.gov.ae/ ; Dubai Health: https://www.dha.gov.ae/ ; VERIFY which applies).
Paired data: for each participant, a laboratory semen analysis from the same sample (within 1 hour), plus the home capture. Minimum 150 participants as a first target, spread over both setups and at least 3 phone models. Collected by donor, so no donor appears in both training and testing.
Reported: sensitivity for Low bands, specificity, the false-Typical rate (target under 5%), the share of Unclear results, and confidence intervals, per setup and per phone model. We publish what we measure. If it is lower than 85 to 90%, we publish the lower number.
External test: at least one setup and one clinic not used in training.
Drift monitoring: weekly checks of Unclear rate, quality-gate failure rate, and lab agreement on a sample of referred users.
A named person can suspend the feature in minutes (feature flag).
Reference evidence for expectations (summaries, verify before quoting): Hagobogo Pro, SpermCell, YO (FDA K241628) and LensHooke X3 PRO (FDA K242830). All validated phone systems use a clip-on lens and a fixed-depth chamber. A bare phone camera has no validation.

6.13 Regulatory note
Treat the semen module as potential Software as a Medical Device in the UAE. Sources disagree on whether the Emirates Drug Establishment or MOHAP is the authority (Federal Decree-Law 38/2024); the DoH and DHA have their own AI policies. This is not legal advice. Before any public release, the owner must get written advice from a UAE regulatory adviser. The prototype stays within “pilot with consenting volunteers, not a public medical release” (A3).

