PART 8 — QUESTIONNAIRE, SCREENING AND PLAN
8.1 Questionnaire (F4)
Content: use the approved questionnaire (5 blocks, 26 questions) from the product specification without change, with “Prefer not to say” and “Not sure” on every question. Store with definition_version. The client renders from the definition JSON so a content change needs no app release. Arabic text comes from text_ar after clinical review.

8.2 Screening engine (F5, F6)
Deterministic, versioned, unit tested. Input: confirmed answers, confirmed lab values, last valid semen run(s), plan adherence flags (never decisive). Output: colour, urgency (Routine, Timely, Urgent), reasons, used, missing, next action, rule version.

Missing information is not “normal” and is not automatically Yellow. The rules say what to do.
Green means no concern found from the information available. It is never proof of fertility.
Wearable data never changes a colour.
Urgent answers always show the approved urgent text immediately and on the device (local copy for offline).
A new input creates a new run. History is kept.
Rule-set changes are released as a separate artefact with clinical approval and rollback.
8.3 74-day plan (F9)
Reason: the sperm production cycle is about 74 days. Plan templates come from the product specification. Rules: one plan version per user; daily actions are created for the user’s local date (store UTC and IANA time zone); missed days never reset the plan; progress text such as “Good day” or “Not enough information”, never a score; no automatic medication, supplement or strenuous-exercise advice.

