PART 13 — SECURITY, PRIVACY, DATA HANDLING, LOGGING
13.1 Rules
ID
Rule
P1
TLS everywhere. Managed identities for service to service. No keys in code.
P2
Every request is scoped by UserId from the validated token. Test cross-user access at API, repository, worker and AI-tool layers.
P3
Personal identifiers never go to a service outside UAE North. De-identified, confirmed values may, if listed as a Region exception.
P4
Logs never contain report text, values, symptoms, prompts, model answers, phone numbers, tokens or SAS URLs. Application Insights telemetry processors redact.
P5
The random username is the only identifier shown. No real name collected.
P6
Staff cannot browse user records. Support access is by explicit, time-limited user grant and is audited.
P7
Reports and videos are stored only with consent and are deletable. No WORM retention on user health files.
P8
Uploads go to quarantine first. Never read as clean until the scan finishes.
P9
Direct-to-Blob upload (if used) uses short-lived user-delegation SAS limited to one blob, upload-only, never logged. Otherwise stream through the API.
P10
Storage with private endpoints where the SKU allows; anonymous access off.
13.2 What we store with consent (reports)
For each report: original file, full extraction JSON, confirmed summary JSON, values table, audit trail of AI value vs user value, and the check-screen image reference. The user sees all of it in the app and can delete it.

13.3 Where the JSON lives
report-json/{user_id}/{doc_id}/extraction.json (every text element the OCR returned, with positions and confidence, header region masked) and summary.json (Section 5.5). Both are in the UAE North storage account.

13.4 UAE obligations to confirm (not legal advice)
Counsel must confirm: Federal Decree-Law 45/2021 (personal data protection) and its executive regulations; the federal health-data law on ICT in health fields (Federal Law 2/2019) including local storage and retention; DoH Abu Dhabi and DHA Dubai requirements including AI policies and mobile health app registration; Malaffi (Abu Dhabi) and NABIDH (Dubai) only if clinic exchange is added. Start points: https://u.ae/en/about-the-uae/digital-uae/data/data-protection-laws ; https://www.doh.gov.ae/ ; https://www.dha.gov.ae/ .

13.5 Deletion lifecycle
On “Delete this report/video/all my data”: mark deleted; remove blobs and versions after soft-delete window; remove derived rows (values, summaries, observations, caches, conversation memory, search indexes if any, exports); keep a minimal audit record that deletion happened; explain backup expiry and any legal retention exception in plain words.

13.6 Research opt-in
Off by default. When on, de-identified data may be used to improve models. A user can withdraw; future use stops. Videos for model training need a separate, explicit consent.

PART 14 — DEVOPS, TESTING, RELEASE
14.1 CI/CD
Infrastructure in Bicep. GitHub Actions with OIDC federation to Azure (no stored secrets).
Pipeline: lint, unit tests, integration tests with a test SQL container, contract tests against the API spec, dependency and secret scans, mobile build (EAS), accessibility and RTL snapshot checks.
Database migrations by expand-and-contract. Staging uses synthetic data only.
Screening rules, clinical content, prompts, quality-gate thresholds and model versions are separate, versioned artefacts with approval and rollback.
14.2 Test plan (all mandatory)
Screening rule boundary tests for every colour.
Numeric leakage test (R1): no pipeline number reaches the client.
Semen pipeline: golden videos for each outcome (Typical, Low, Unclear, no sperm, too dense, blurry, drift, missing calibration, unknown depth). Each must reach a result state.
Chain-break test: inject a failure into each stage S0 to S13; the session must reach its documented fallback.
Idempotency: replay every message twice.
Consent withdrawal mid-job.
Report pipeline: malformed, oversized, password-protected, scanned, rotated, Arabic, low-light files; auto-masking of header text.
Cross-user access (API, workers, AI tools).
Ask agent: grounding test set (each number must be traceable); navigation catalogue test; urgent-word routing; no-diagnosis test.
Arabic RTL on every screen; screen reader; large text.
Offline and weak-signal flows.
Load: 200 concurrent sessions in staging; queue age alert.
Restore test of SQL point-in-time recovery and blob soft delete.
Security: dependency scan, secrets scan, an external penetration test before pilot.
14.3 Monitoring
Dashboards: API latency and errors, queue age, dead-letter count, stage failure rate, Unclear rate, quality-gate failure rate, upload resume rate, Ask fallback rate, LLM latency. Alerts page the on-call developer. No health content in telemetry.

