PART 16 — MVP BACKLOG: EPICS, STORIES, ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
Format: Story → Acceptance criteria (AC). Each AC is testable.

E1 — Onboarding, accounts and consent (F1, F2, F3)
E1-S1 As a new user I pick a language and see a privacy summary. AC: English is default; if phone language is Arabic a “Switch to Arabic?” prompt shows; layout flips to RTL; summary text is under 120 words.
E1-S2 As a user I get a random username and sign in without a real name. AC: no field asks for name; username unique; token stored in secure storage; sign-in via PKCE.
E1-S3 As a user I can set a recovery method later. AC: warning is shown if none is set; recovery restores the same UserId.
E1-S4 As a user I control each consent separately. AC: eight switches per Section 3.2; withdrawal blocks the related API within one request; version change prompts again.
E2 — Questionnaire (F4)
E2-S1 As a user I answer 26 questions in 5 blocks. AC: one question per screen; “Prefer not to say” and “Not sure” on every question; progress saved after each answer; resume works after app kill.
E2-S2 As a user I can change an answer. AC: a new response row; earlier row kept; a new screening run is created.
E3 — Screening and urgent route (F5, F6)
E3-S1 As a user I see a 3-colour bar with the reason. AC: word and icon with colour; reasons, used and missing lists shown; no number or percentage anywhere.
E3-S2 As a user with urgent answers I see approved urgent text at once. AC: shown within 1 second, works offline; server re-evaluates.
E3-S3 As a user in Red I can book a diagnostic centre. AC: provider list; referral summary preview; sharing has provider, scope and expiry.
E3-S4 Rules versioning. AC: each run stores rule version; changing rules does not alter old runs.
E4 — Plan and Today (F9)
E4-S1 As a user I get a 74-day plan. AC: actions per local date; unique constraint prevents duplicates; missed days do not reset the plan.
E4-S2 As a user I get neutral reminders. AC: no health words in notification text.
E5 — Data rights (F15)
E5-S1 Export. AC: package of all user data within 24 hours; link expires in 7 days.
E5-S2 Delete. AC: all blobs, rows, caches and memory removed per Section 13.5; confirmation shown; deletion audit kept without health content.
E6 — Report vault (F7)
E6-S1 Privacy guidance before upload. AC: note about folding, covering or cropping is shown on every upload; crop tool with blackout works.
E6-S2 Upload and scan. AC: file types and size enforced; quarantine first; infected or invalid files rejected with the defined message.
E6-S3 Extraction and masking. AC: values, units, ranges, dates extracted from the golden report set with at least 95% of fields correct on clean PDFs (target, measure and publish); header personal data never appears in report_values, summary or LLM input.
E6-S4 User check and confirm. AC: original and extracted fields side by side; low-confidence highlighted; unconfirmed values never reach decisions or the agent.
E6-S5 Summary JSON. AC: schema v1 validates; exact values and dates preserved; plain_text_summary numbers all present in values.
E6-S6 Manual entry fallback. AC: if extraction fails the user can type values and still reach Summarised.
E6-S7 Report list and delete. AC: delete removes original, JSON and derived rows.
E7 — Ask agent and navigation (F12)
E7-S1 As a user I ask about app features and get a button. AC: the seven navigation rows in Section 7.3 open the correct screens; coming-soon features are named as such.
E7-S2 As a user I ask about my report. AC: answer cites report date; every number traceable to confirmed values; works only with reports_ai; with consent off the agent offers to open the Reports screen.
E7-S3 Safety. AC: urgent words trigger approved text first; the agent never states fertile or infertile, never gives doses; never gives a number for a home semen result.
E7-S4 Degraded mode. AC: with Ask:LlmMode = TemplatesOnly the app still answers navigation and result questions.
E8 — Nutrition and Noon (F10)
E8-S1 As a user I see today’s food suggestions. AC: from reviewed catalogue; allergy tags respected; Arabic names present.
E8-S2 As a user I choose items and get a Noon list. AC: agent asks first; each item has a search link and a copy button; list has a copy-all; only the item name is in the URL.
E8-S3 Coming-soon toggle. AC: shown in Settings as disabled with the badge; no network call; no stored data.
E8-S4 Link check. AC: NoonLinkBuilder pattern verified manually and recorded; a health-check job opens one sample link weekly and alerts on failure.
E9 — Wearables (F11)
E9-S1 As a user I connect Health Connect or HealthKit. AC: per-category permission; disconnect stops sync; missing values stay NULL.
E9-S2 As a user I see 7 and 28-day sleep and heart trends. AC: source labelled; one-line note that this is not a fertility measurement.
